{"name":"Hera Blue","hex":"#7777ee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hera","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female hero; a heroine, especially in lesbian or feminist circles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hera"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hera","blocks":[{"text":"In ancient Greek religion, Hera is the goddess of marriage, women, and family, and the protector of women during childbirth. In Greek mythology, she is queen among the twelve Olympians on Mount Olympus, sister and wife of Zeus, and daughter of the Titans Cronus and Rhea. One of her defining characteristics in myth is her jealous and vengeful nature in dealing with any who offended her, especially Zeus's numerous adulterous lovers and illegitimate offspring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Hera_Campana_Louvre_Ma2283.jpg/330px-Hera_Campana_Louvre_Ma2283.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hera","wikidata":"Q38012"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Marriage_of_Zeus_and_Hera_%28detail%29_Pompeian_Art.jpg/500px-Marriage_of_Zeus_and_Hera_%28detail%29_Pompeian_Art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Marriage_of_Zeus_and_Hera_%28detail%29_Pompeian_Art.jpg/1280px-Marriage_of_Zeus_and_Hera_%28detail%29_Pompeian_Art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Marriage_of_Zeus_and_Hera_%28detail%29_Pompeian_Art.jpg/500px-Marriage_of_Zeus_and_Hera_%28detail%29_Pompeian_Art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hera on an antique fresco from Pompeii","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarriage_of_Zeus_and_Hera_(detail)_Pompeian_Art.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Temple_of_Hera_-_Agrigento_-_Italy_2015.JPG/500px-Temple_of_Hera_-_Agrigento_-_Italy_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Temple_of_Hera_-_Agrigento_-_Italy_2015.JPG/1280px-Temple_of_Hera_-_Agrigento_-_Italy_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Temple_of_Hera_-_Agrigento_-_Italy_2015.JPG/500px-Temple_of_Hera_-_Agrigento_-_Italy_2015.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai